{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QuNWJFqcZj2QyzMsrR2XNp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity and R&D control system. Grounded claims from the repo:\n\n- **Purpose:** A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that manages tasks, projects, and ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) â€” with markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`) as the single source of truth, no database.\n\n- **What it ships (core app):** `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and reads/writes the markdown directly. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task lifecycle (add/done/cancel/save/restore/capture) and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle:** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, all as plain-text markdown edits, logged to `logs/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **R&D \"Cockpit\" surface (the major build effort):** A per-project control surface that runs the **trio** â€” researchPrime (Research) â†’ Crucible (Planning) â†’ Foreman (Build) â€” as durable, isolated, server-side **Claude Code / Gemini terminal sessions**. It's been built across four versions (v2 sessions/summaries/grass, v3 \"Mission Control\" ConPTY terminals + git-worktree isolation + stacking windows, v4 \"Project Cockpit\" â€” current branch work). It ships real ConPTY terminals (xterm.js + the one declared native dep `pywinpty`), per-lane status-light tiles with inline expanding panels, engine toggle (claudeâ†”gemini), cached/validated AI summaries, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, a grass-idea board, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Self-verification:** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM (Task Scheduler), parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching port 8777), and writing `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **Constraints it holds to:** Python stdlib only (sole exception: lazy `pywinpty` for terminals), single folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), all files plain-text/Cowork-accessible, branded as a \"Ghost World Labs\" tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\".\n\nThe current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) is mid-work on the v4.1 cockpit render â€” the project window now renders lanes as Paradigm-2 tiles replacing the older effort-card kanban."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb30dcdf-4ae3-4b60-b3f2-bc367b285197","uuid":"b7ea353b-8c6e-4f03-9a5e-903710d9cb4d","request_id":"req_011Cc2Gt2pGwWkDhiRrysMQX"}
